# What must NOT go into the build context.
#
# Without this file Docker ships the entire working directory to the daemon —
# including frontend/node_modules and frontend/dist. Both are actively harmful:
#
#   node_modules is installed on Windows, so it carries win32 binaries for
#   esbuild and rollup. The Dockerfile installs Linux ones with `npm ci` and the
#   later `COPY frontend/ ./` then copies the Windows tree straight over them.
#
#   dist is a build output. Shipping a stale one into the image and hoping the
#   build overwrites it is exactly the sort of thing that makes a deploy
#   "succeed" while serving yesterday's JavaScript.
#
# It also makes the context a few hundred megabytes instead of a few, which is
# most of the build time on a small server.

.git
.gitignore

# Node
**/node_modules
frontend/dist

# Python
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.venv
venv

# Local data that must never end up in an image
.env
*.db
backend/uploads
backend/data
backend/catalog_images

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
